From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:57:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(antigravity): gate shell commands by Omnigent policy and
 permission mode

The Antigravity SDK's default policy, confirm_run_command(), denies its
run_command tool outright, and the harness reported that denial as a turn
error, so every turn in which Gemini ran a shell command failed with
`Denied by policy "confirm_run_command"`.

Allow every tool at the SDK policy layer and gate run_command in a
PreToolCallDecideHook, the way the cursor and claude-sdk harnesses gate
their native tools: Omnigent TOOL_CALL policies first (DENY refuses, ASK
asks), then executor.config.permission_mode (auto, the default, and
bypassPermissions run the command; any other mode asks on an approval
card). A refusal fails that tool call with its reason; the SDK reports it
as an ERROR step and lets the model continue, so that step is no longer
treated as a turn failure. Approval cards now say "Antigravity" instead
of "Claude".

Upstream issue omnigent-ai/omnigent#8484 tracks the bug; the open
omnigent-ai/omnigent#8497 routes the SDK's ask_user handler to the
approval card instead and does not evaluate Omnigent policies. Not
proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
